BCP640-Cold Lake Museum. Elevation 566.823 m
BRASS CAP 0.3 M N OF MP. LOCATED IN GRASS ON NORTH EDGE OF HIGH HILL 18.2 M NORTH WEST OF POWER POLE NORTH OF FROST FENCE. 19.9 M NORTH OF EAST WEST FROSTFENCE ALONG NORTH BOUNDARY OF RADAR INSTALLATION</groundspeak:encoded_hints>
      <groundspeak:logs>
        <groundspeak:log id="697250138">
          <groundspeak:date>2017-06-24T20:00:00</groundspeak:date>
          <groundspeak:type>Found it</groundspeak:type>
          <groundspeak:finder id="836983">Coolcat21</groundspeak:finder>
          <groundspeak:text encoded="True">&lt;p&gt;BCP640 - Cold Lake Museum

Posted: N54° 26.129' W110° 10.933'

(FOUND)&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;The Nuvi really came through for me getting me to this one because it is a little out of the way.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;One the way up the hill to the museum I saw a Bull Terrier running up the hill along the road in front of me. Hmmm. that's odd. That's not your usual out-doorsy kind dog. It turns out the owner was &quot;walking&quot; his dog by driving up the hill in his truck and making the dog run after the truck behind him. I didn't know whether to laugh or cry.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;Finding the cap was pretty straight forward though. I smiled about that.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;On the way down the hill leaving the area, sure enough, the truck was driving up the hill again with the dog running behind it.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;Wow. Just wow.&lt;/p&gt;

          </groundspeak:text>
        </groundspeak:log>
        <groundspeak:log id="620969562">
          <groundspeak:date>2016-07-23T20:00:00</groundspeak:date>
          <groundspeak:type>Found it</groundspeak:type>
          <groundspeak:finder id="3355355">CachingCarolandHugh</groundspeak:finder>
          <groundspeak:text encoded="True">&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;BCP640 – Cold Lake Museum&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Posted: N54º 26.129   W110º 10.933 

Elevation: 566.8 M&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;GPSr:    N 54º 26.129  W110º 10.930

Elevation: 558&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;We had gone up to Cold Lake on Tuesday July 5th to attend the Sails, Rails &amp; Tails 2016 (WESTCAN6) Mega event. Then tayed over at the RV park we were at, for another week to do some more caching and take in the Cold Lake Air Show the following weekend. We logged a lot of caches found and with the satellite event in places like Elk Point and Glendon were also able to find some of the Brass Caps in Cold Lake and area.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;...CachingCarolandHugh &lt;img src="/images/icons/icon_smile_approve.gif" border="0" align="middle" /&gt;&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/p&gt;

          </groundspeak:text>
        </groundspeak:log>
        <groundspeak:log id="618727471">
          <groundspeak:date>2016-07-10T20:00:00</groundspeak:date>
          <groundspeak:type>Found it</groundspeak:type>
          <groundspeak:finder id="946600">Black Shark</groundspeak:finder>
          <groundspeak:text encoded="True">&lt;p&gt;BCP640 Cold Lake Museum&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;Many revving dirt bikes and an industrial weed whacker shattered the quiet here.  The weed whacker operator paused to let us pass and greeted us pleasantly as we headed down the well trod geotrail.  The guide post is easily visible over the tall grass and, with so many recent visits, the cap only needed a few blades of grass moved before the pictures could be taken.  While walking back along the chain link fence, we thought we heard a shout over the din and looked back to see a GPS toting fellow on the other side.  He asked about the cap and we pointed out the marker.  All he had to do was get on the right side of the fence! Thanks for the cap with an interesting perspective of some the planes and squadron emblems.&lt;/p&gt;

          </groundspeak:text>
        </groundspeak:log>
        <groundspeak:log id="617233642">
          <groundspeak:log_wpt lat="54.435483" lon="-110.182217" />
          <groundspeak:date>2016-07-10T20:00:00</groundspeak:date>
          <groundspeak:type>Found it</groundspeak:type>
          <groundspeak:finder id="11091667">WillowZilla</groundspeak:finder>
          <groundspeak:text encoded="True">&lt;p&gt;BCP640 - Cold Lake Museum

One of my missions for the MEGA event SRT was to grab all the brass cap's in town, this guy completed the circuit. Once we hit GZish, we all parked at the gate to the museum, with another vehicle, which turned out to be someone just waiting for a co-worker? to open the gate and let them in.  I'm sure they were wondering what's up with the crazies driving up and ditching their vehicles to wander off into the tall grass :)&lt;/p&gt;

          </groundspeak:text>
        </groundspeak:log>
